.\" M4KK1 4P1 - quell.8
.TH QUELL 8 "2026-07-22" "M4KK1 1.0" "M4KK1 System Administration"
.SH NAME
quell \- execute a command with prime group privileges
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quell
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute a command with root privileges (euid=0). The caller must be a member of the prime group (GID 1001). This is the M4KK1 alternative to sudo.
.SH EXAMPLE
.TP
.B quell mount /dev/yafs0 /mnt
Mount a filesystem
.TP
.B quell usermod -a --group prime alice
Add alice to the prime group
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usermod (8),
.BR groupmod (8),
.BR passwd (8)
